sparky-stereo-throw (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A live stream a real receiver plays (queue row 81, part D, measured on a real Chromecast): the picture keeps
    coming on a still screen (KPipeWire encodes the last frame again at the mode's rate; before, a still screen
    gave two pictures and then none, and the receiver waited for ever); the sound is a choice on the device's page
    (PCM 24 or 16 bit, FLAC, Opus, AAC, Vorbis, MP3, and Dolby Digital or Dolby Digital Plus 5.1), by default the
    best stereo sound the stream carries that has not failed on that device, 24-bit PCM in Matroska; what a device
    played, or did not start playing, is kept for it by its identity.
  * A Throw the device does not play within 60 seconds is ended and said with what the device reported, never left
    as "throwing" before a loading screen; every Cast message is in the debug log, the stream's token taken out.

